reported as errors before any other logic | Invalid line numbers are masked by 
"full file read" logic |\n| Callers should get clear feedback about invalid 
parameters | Callers might think they provided valid parameters but got 
misleading response |\n| Error handling should be consistent regardless of file 
read status | Different code paths for "full" vs partial reads |\n\n## Root 
Cause\nThe `should_read_file` method has this validation order:\n1. First checks
if file exists in recent files\n2. Then checks if file was read "full" (early 
return with False)\n3. **Only then** validates line number parameters\n\nThis 
means invalid line numbers (e.g., start=0, end=-1) are not validated when a file
was read "full", because the method returns early at step 2.\n\n## Fix 
Plan\nMove line number validation to happen BEFORE checking if file was read 
"full". The validation should:\n1. Check start/end parameters for type and value
validity (positive integers, start <= end)\n2. Only after validation, check file
